{
  "id": "part-object",
  "term": "part-object",
  "definition": "In object relations psychoanalysis, a part-object is a simplified mental representation of another person organized around a limited, emotionally charged aspect, such as being experienced as wholly good or wholly bad. The packet describes these part-objects as early-formed prior models that can shape perception and relationships, sometimes overriding more realistic awareness of the whole person.",
